{
  "abstract": "Pure core Lean 4 (zero Mathlib imports) formalization answering Padrol–Philippe (Combinatorica 44, 2024) Question 7.21 in the negative in every VC-dimension rank r >= 4 via window sweep acycloids W(n, m). Alongside the counterexample family (for 3 <= m <= n/2, starting at W(6, 3) with 240 permutations and rank 4), the compared theorems establish exact cardinality and simple allowable/sweep-acycloid structure, the full shattered-forest characterization and VC dimension, failure of matroid augmentation, three independent non-matroidal obstructions (oriented-matroid minor contraction, a da Silva potential-sweep witness, and the Knauer–Marc excluded partial-cube minor Q_{n - 2m + 4}^{--}(n - 2m + 4) together with Tamura's C_0 match at W(6, 3)), and exact realizability for m <= 2 over every linearly ordered commutative ring with 0 < 1. Main results: 14 of 14 in Lean (100%) · Abstract claims: 14 of 14 in Lean (100%) · 2 supporting lemmas (16 of 16 numbered claims compared in Challenge.lean, 72 of 72 verified declarations in Verify.lean; zero sorry, zero native_decide, standard axioms only). Uses the tope reading of Padrol–Philippe Definition 7.13(i) (extension to all covectors cited from Section 7.4 and Lemma 7.17). Rank 3 remains open. Companion page: https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/sweep-acycloids-not-oriented-matroids.",
